Indian Handicrafts Industry — Market Statistics
Industry Overview

India's handicrafts sector is an important part of the country's creative economy, providing employment to more than 6.4 million artisans. Around 64% of the workforce consists of women, highlighting the sector's importance as a source of livelihood and economic participation.

India has a highly diverse handicraft ecosystem, with more than 455 craft categories and 318 GI-tagged handicraft products. The industry is largely rural-based, with production concentrated in artisan clusters across different regions of the country.

Market Size

According to data cited by IBEF from the Export Promotion Council for Handicrafts (EPCH), the Indian handicrafts market was valued at approximately US$4.56 billion in 2024 and is projected to reach US$8.19 billion by 2033, representing a projected CAGR of 6.39%.

IBEF also cites an IMARC estimate placing the market at US$4.85 billion in 2025, with a projected value of US$8.29 billion by 2034 at a CAGR of 6.13% during 2026–2034.
Export Statistics

India's handicraft exports, excluding hand-knotted carpets, reached approximately ₹33,424.18 crore (US$3.783 billion) in FY2025–26. The FY2026 figure is based on provisional EPCH data covering 179 ITC HS codes.

For comparison, exports in FY2024–25 were approximately ₹33,122.79 crore (US$3.916 billion). In rupee terms, exports increased by 0.91% in FY2025–26.

The major export categories in FY2025–26 included:

Export Category	Export Value

Miscellaneous Handicrafts   	- US$1,148.54 million
Woodwares                     -	US$840.39 million
Art Metalwares                -	US$505.06 million
Embroidered & Crocheted Goods -	US$484.92 million
Handprinted Textiles & Scarves-	US$443.24 million
